# UI completion gate

Before marking **substantial** UI work complete (skip for trivial copy/CSS tweaks):

1. Run relevant project checks that exist (`npm run lint`, typecheck, build as applicable).
2. Prefer Impeccable for visual craft verification: `/impeccable critique` and/or `/impeccable audit` on the changed surface; optional `npx impeccable detect src/`.
3. For independent second opinion on rendered UX/hierarchy (not the same as detector rules), invoke `visual-reviewer` once — do not also rerun a full `visual-quality-audit` skill unless the user asks.
4. For accessibility depth beyond Impeccable `audit`, invoke `accessibility-reviewer` once.
5. Inspect browser output when tools are available; check one narrow and one desktop viewport when responsive work is in scope.
6. Fix high-severity findings or explicitly explain why they remain.
7. Report exactly what was checked. Never claim visual/browser/Impeccable verification without evidence.
